<%# What the footer's loop sheet holds: one card per loop that is being worked
    right now, and a sentence when there is none.

    A loop is not a thing this conversation can watch the way it watches a
    turn: its progress is a file on disk, written by a run in a worktree of its
    own. So a card says the two things a reader opens it for -- how many
    iterations of how many it has spent, and what is left of its budget -- and
    nothing else. The goal is cut to one line above them, because a card is a
    glance, and the whole of it is on the tooltip.

    There was more here, and every line of it was a word repeating what the
    reader already knew: the loop's id (they asked for one loop), its status
    (the panel draws only what is running), what it has spent (the same fact as
    what is left, said twice) and when it last moved (a clock ticking on a panel
    nobody leaves open). Two figures answer the question; the rest was noise
    around them.

    The rows are drawn on the page and then again by the poll in _loop_sheet,
    which is why nothing here talks to the store: it is handed the rows
    (see Web::Loops#loop_rows) and only places them.

    A card wears one mark that is not a figure: the ring in front of the goal,
    drawn while the loop's lease is held. It is the only thing on the card that
    says "something is happening now" — the numbers move once per iteration,
    which can be minutes — and it is decided by loop_rows, not here. -%>
<% if loops.empty? -%>
  <p class="usage-note"><%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.empty")) %></p>
<% else -%>
  <ul class="loop-rows">
<% loops.each do |loop| -%>
    <li class="loop">
      <span class="loop-goal" title="<%= h(loop[:goal]) %>"><%- if loop[:running] -%><span class="loop-mark" title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.running_one")) %>" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.running_one")) %>"><%= View.spinner_mark("loop-spinner") %></span><%- end -%><span class="loop-goal-text"><%= h(loop[:goal]) %></span></span>
      <span class="loop-facts">
        <%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.iterations", done: loop[:iterations], max: loop[:max_iterations])) %>
        · <%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.remaining", left: num(loop[:remaining]), total: num(loop[:max_tokens]))) %>
      </span>
    </li>
<% end -%>
  </ul>
<% end -%>
